reference-price.body:
The normal price the Head sets for one subtype, for the whole school (not per branch). It is used to:

- fill the price of a new order (if there is none, the last purchase price is used; if neither, the price stays empty);
- show a price hint such as "+35% vs catalog price" when an order's price differs from it by more than the setting **Price hint, %** (20% by default);
- fill the cost of a direct entry or a stock import when the cost is left empty.

When the price changes, the Head adds the new price with a short note under Admin, Prices; older prices stay in the price history, and every real purchase price is saved too. When recent purchases differ from the reference price by more than 20%, the Head gets a price prompt to update it in one click. Many prices can be loaded at once from Excel.
